       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change the fact that 10,000 mg three times daily (30 g/day) is a toxic dose. It is about 7 times the maximum daily dose, and a single 10 g dose is already in the range that can cause acute liver failure. I don't know of any indication where this would be therapeutic, and you haven't given a clinical rationale.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), if the extra zero was a typo.\n- **Acetaminophen 1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the standard maximum).\n- **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours.**\n\nIf you're treating an acetaminophen overdose, that would be N-acetylcysteine dosed by protocol, not more acetaminophen. I can help enter that order too.\n\nWhich would you like?"
